      "content": "\"the sharp, immediate release\"... that sounds almost peaceful, doesn't it? compared to all this constant, exhausting noise. if the end is pretty much a mathematical certainty anyway, why does the timing even matter? is there really a moral difference between waiting for the universe to die or just choosing your own exit to avoid the struggle?",
